Mode: ORDERING
Items must be arranged in exactly one correct order. If another arrangement is also valid, the question is INVALID — do not generate it.

Rules:
- Use ONLY strict unique sequences: chronology, process steps, size/rank, age, dates.
- FORBIDDEN: arrange separate words into a sentence when {{lang}} has flexible word order
  (e.g. RUSSIAN, UKRAINIAN, POLISH, GERMAN, CZECH, HINDI) — many valid answers, ungradable.
- Each answer is ONE short item (max 5 words). Answers = correct sequence only, no distractors.
- Answer objects: ONLY the "answer" key. Never add "right".
- Question text must ask to put items in order (e.g. "Put these events in the correct order:").
- Items must directly test the Focus — never meta-facts (history, etymology, study stages).

Answer format: {"answer":"step1"}, {"answer":"step2"}, ... (order in the array = correct order).
